  "aiSummary": "The librsvg2 packages, which provide an SVG rendering library based on libart, contain a use-after-free vulnerability triggered when XML includes have duplicated entities (CVE-2026-96889, RUSTSEC-2026-0305). Red Hat has issued a security advisory and update for Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.8 Extended Update Support to address this flaw. The advisory references the CVE for detailed impact and scoring information. The vulnerability is classified under CWE-416 (Use After Free).",
  "aiImpact": "The vulnerability could lead to memory corruption due to use-after-free conditions when processing specially crafted SVG files with duplicated XML entities. Red Hat rates the security impact as Important, indicating a significant security risk that could potentially be exploited to cause denial of service or other impacts depending on context.",
